~~~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOW TO EDIT THIS PAGE
#
# 1. Replace every occurrence of
#        YOUR-GITHUB-USER/YOUR-COURSE-REPO
#    with the user and repository that hosts your course files, e.g.
#        phuongluuvo/course-materials
#    Use your editor's "replace all" -- it appears once per file link.
#
# 2. Two ways to link a file in another repository:
#      * the raw file, which downloads or opens directly:
#            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/USER/REPO/main/FOLDER/file.pdf
#      * the GitHub page for the file, which shows a preview first:
#            https://github.com/USER/REPO/blob/main/FOLDER/file.pdf
#
# 3. To add a dropdown, copy this block and change the title and the links.
#    Leave a blank line before and after the ~~~
#
# ~~~
# {}{raw}
# <details class="materials">
# <summary>Title of the group</summary>
# <ul>
# <li><a href="https://example.com/file.pdf" target="blank">Label of the file (PDF)</a></li>
# </ul>
# </details>
# ~~~
#
# 4. To add a whole course, copy an entire == section above. The course
#    information box is a normal jemdoc info block (~~~ ... ~~~), not HTML.
#
# 5. Keep target="blank" on every external link: the test-suite requires it,
#    and it makes the file open in a new tab instead of replacing your site.
#
# 6. Write &amp; for a literal ampersand and &ndash; for a dash inside the HTML
#    blocks; the stylesheet picks up class="materials" automatically.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
